# The llama.cpp pins, one b-build per host class, and the repository of ggml's images. A class's
# build serves each of its flavors: host/llama.sh names the server image server-<flavor>-<build> in
# LLAMA_REPOSITORY, and llama_pin (host/llama-release.sh) reads the class's pin. strix-halo (the
# Framework; rocm and vulkan) runs the b-build named ("Nightly build:") in the notes of the latest
# semver release, LLAMA_RELEASE. In spike-model-engines, gb10 (gb10-1; cuda13) runs b12063, a
# b-build past that release, which its verification adopted (spike-hosting-upgrades,
# docs/findings/verify-gb10-1.md there). Sourced by host/llama-release.sh.
#
# This file is the root's own, not a copy: it is spike-model-engines dfc1d3d's llama.env with gb10's
# pin held at b12098 for gb10-2 (gb10-2-align), every other variable as upstream sets it. b12100 and
# later (llama.cpp #31620 and #31639) match an -hf quant tag only after a -, . or /, so set A's
# vision model, google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf:Q4_0, whose file is
# gemma-4-26B_q4_0-it.gguf, can't resolve. b12098 (149f5641b) is the newest build with #31391, the
# fix for the idle-slot stall, and a server-cuda13 image.
LLAMA_RELEASE=v0.8.0
LLAMA_BUILD_GB10=b12098
LLAMA_BUILD_STRIX_HALO=b11960
LLAMA_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp
